<%# The signed-in right side of the navbar. This SHADOWS studio-engine's
    components/_user_nav (a host view wins in this non-isolated engine) for ONE
    reason: the name. The engine partial prints current_user.display_name, which
    in Cyvasse is a real name first ("Guest 4821"), kept for email greetings and
    the admin pages. The navbar shows the player's one public name instead,
    User#player_name ("Guest_4821"), the name the board, the leaderboard and chat
    show (task cyvasse-contrast-and-names; test/integration/navbar_account_test.rb).
    studio-engine 0.79.0 has no setting, local or helper for that name.

    Everything else here the engine partial now does itself (0.79.0,
    engine-navbar-phone-polish): the theme toggle md+ only, one account link,
    the avatar alone on a phone with the name as screen-reader text, and the
    desktop sidebar button through extra_icons_html. Cyvasse players have no
    balance, wallet or level, so the engine's second row never renders here.
    Keep this markup in step with the engine's signed-in branch, and delete
    this file once the engine partial takes its display name from a hook. %>
<% name = current_user.player_name %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
  <%# The engine's navbar hands its desktop link-sidebar button in here as
      extra_icons_html (layouts/_navbar). Without it a
      desktop has no way into the sidebar: Inbox, Pieces, Rules, About, Admin. %>
  <%= local_assigns[:extra_icons_html] %>
  <%= render "components/admin_dropdown" unless respond_to?(:studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu?) && studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu? %>
  <span class="hidden md:flex" data-nav-theme-toggle="desktop"><%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %></span>
  <%= link_to profile_path, class: "group flex items-center gap-2 flex-shrink-0 hover:opacity-80 transition", data: { nav_account: true } do %>
    <span class="sr-only md:not-sr-only md:max-w-40"><span class="block truncate text-right text-heading font-semibold text-base leading-none transition group-hover:text-primary" data-nav-name><%= name %></span></span>
    <span class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center" aria-hidden="true">
      <%= render "components/avatar", user: current_user, size: "nav" %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
</div>
